{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/414338-exploit-errata-possession","id":414338,"title":"Exploit Errata : Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-21T13:10:27-08:00","id":414338,"title":"Exploit Errata : Possession","content":"After watching American Horror Story, Asylum, I became really interested in the Exploit Possession! However, it's not very fleshed out, so I decided to add some stuff to it as various edge cases popped up in our games and we made rulings. Feel free to critique the finer points, I want a 'no pagecount limit' version of the power that's true to the spirit of the original and retains the feel of a demonic possession. Instead of doing a full fluff write up, I'm just going to present the ideas like this...<br /> <br /> Demons are not injured by Twilight weapons and do not manifest in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Demons who are possessing individuals may spoof as normal to seem like \u2018normal\u2019 soul parts / thoughts.<br /> <br /> Demons who spoof while using Possession use Primum in lieu of Cover.<br /> <br /> Assuming a proper spoof, particularly acute mental senses like telepathy may identify the Demon as a repressed personality or part of a personality within the victim, but not supernatural tampering.<br /> <br /> Demons who as possessing individuals \u2018hide\u2019 in the \u2018soul cavity\u2019 and are thus difficult to dislodge. Soul Attacks like a Strix bite do not 'eat' them.<br /> <br /> Demons who are possessing individuals may elect to observe, effectively returning control to the host. This requires no roll.<br /> <br /> Regaining control of the host is a reflex action that requires a single success on Resolve + Composure. Supernatural beings resist as normal.<br /> <br /> Demons may freely use Embeds and Exploits for the benefit of the victim.<br /> <br /> Use of 'Never There', 'Homogenous Memory' and 'Without a Trace' can create situations where the host has lost time and misremembers events.<br /> <br /> Demons do not need to roll to use these embeds on a host as long as the initial possession is effective.<br /> <br /> Demons who undergo Compromise while possessing must use the 'Demon' conditions appropriate to Unchained without cover.<br /> <br /> Possessing a person when they die ejects the Demon in true form with attendant Compromise.<br /> <br /> Being rendered unconscious while possessing a person allows the demon of either ejecting as per death or sharing the unconscious (and helpless) state.<br /> <br /> Possession requires eye contact.<br /> <br /> A victim who is possessed cannot sign pacts or make agreements unless they are not being actively controlled, as per above.<br /> <br /> You cannot possess an unconscious target anymore than you can connect to a powered off computer over the internet.<br /> <br /> Spending one aether allows you to mine the brain for memories on a single topic, as per an Auspex 4 read.<br /> <br /> If the success to possess was normal, then this is a Wits + Investigation at -4.<br /> <br /> If the success to possess was exceptional, this is a Wits + Investigation roll with no penalty.<br /> <br /> ... we have some unofficial errata for other embeds and exploits as well, if people are interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 02-21-2015, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:05:41-08:00","id":414619,"title":"","content":"I like your expansion of the power well enough, though I have a few questions and additional thoughts.<br /> <br /> Did you likewise improve the Manifestation Power? If so: Is it able to use Numina from within a host body now?<br /> <br /> If not: Why have you decided that a Demon's ability to possess should be greater than an Angel's ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T22:12:47-08:00","id":414912,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't improve the default power, but I'd propose a more advanced version that could be used for appropriate entities.<br /> <br /> I don't think embeds and exploits should be as hard to use in a possessed victim as numina. Ephemeral entities have a harder time bringing power into the real world in general than unchained do. They have a harder time forcing the power of a spirit through a mortal body because those powers are coming from a distant power source and further they aren't usually intended to be used by human-like creatures. Embeds and exploits, on the other hand, are purely physical tricks that are (in some cases) sparked by aether and simply knowing how to do it. They're more natural to the material world and more natural to human-like creatures, because they were designed by Unchained for long term use while hiding in human-like shapes. Numina were not designed under such strict restrictions.<br /> <br /> That said, a more powerful numina that brute forces spiritual powers into a human frame probably should exist for appropriate ephemera, like I said above. Just, in general, Unchained are more advanced at using human husks than Angels are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T07:22:20-08:00","id":415104,"title":"","content":"I disagree and suggest that you are perhaps considering Numina as purely spiritual techniques in the sense that they belong to Spirits themselves, entities alien (albeit sympathetically connected to the natural world) while angels, by the description, are the material World of Darkness' only truly native ephemeral entities. Indeed, Embeds and Exploits themselves are described as shortcuts and hacks to regain some semblance of the ability that the Unchained once possessed as angels, thus implicating angels in the ability to utilise such reality altering powers to a degree higher than the Unchained, not lower.<br /> <br /> That said I never quite understood why either set of beings couldn't use their abilities while successfully inside a host body. I feel like it perhaps should damage the host or loosen the connection but not be entirely prohibited as it makes it difficult, in my mind at least, to perform more traditional tricks that one would see in cinematic possession such as in The Exorcist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}